@@ -0,0 +1,26 @@
+# Render timing
+
+The page loads `render-timing.js` to measure contentful updates caused by user
+interactions, including asynchronous updates and client-side navigations.
+It does not change the site's links into client-side routes.
+
+Listen for `window`'s `render-timing` custom event to consume reports, or read
+`window.renderTiming.getReports()` for the latest 100 reports. Nothing is sent
+over the network. Durations are in milliseconds, relative to the initiating
+interaction, rather than the original page load.
+
+- `interaction-paint`: `interactionId`, `duration`, `element`, `size`. Each larger
+  contentful paint for an interaction produces a new candidate report.
+- `soft-navigation`: `url`, `navigationId`, `interactionId`, `fcpDuration`,
+  `lcpDuration`, `element`, `size`. Finalized on the next soft navigation, when the
+  page becomes hidden, or on page exit. LCP is null when no candidate is available.
+
+`window.renderTiming.supported` exposes browser support. These performance entry
+types have limited availability; unsupported browsers keep working and produce
+no substitute or estimated metrics. This measures contentful updates, not INP
+or initial page-load LCP. Soft-navigation LCP candidates are matched by interaction
+ID, including paints before the URL changed. `window.renderTiming.stop()` drains
+pending records, finalizes the active route, and removes observers and listeners.
+
+Run automated checks with `npm test`. The tests use mocked browser performance
+entries; they do not verify browser-specific entry generation or presentation.
